        tabLabel: 'About',
        pages: [
          {
            title: 'Tau Ngau',
            subtitle: 'Card Game',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Tau Ngau (Bull Fighting) has two main forms. Domino version: 3â€“6 players, banker deals five tiles each; discard three that total a multiple of ten (tiles 4-2 and 2-1 are wild); remaining two tiles give score (mod 10); beat the banker. Card version (Ngau/Gnau): 52-card deck, 2+ players; five cards each; choose three that sum to a multiple of 10 or are three-of-a-kind to be scoring-eligible; two remaining cards give Ox power (face=10, 3s and 6s can be 3 or 6). Hand ranks: Five Dukes, All-Small, Double-Ox, etc. Played in Southeast Asia as casual or gambling game.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Country/Region of Origin: Various\nTime Period: Early 1900s\nHistorical Development: The game evolved from traditional card games in the region\nCultural Significance: Popular social and family game',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Setup',
            subtitle: 'Table, deck, equipment, and deal',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Minimum Players: 3\nMaximum Players: 6\nOptimal Players: 4\nPartnerships: None; onlookers may place side bets.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Type: Double-six domino set (28 tiles)\nNumber of Decks: 1\nWild tiles: 4-2 and 2-1 count as 3 or 6 for discard totals only.',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Double-six domino set\nTable space\nOptional: dice to choose banker',
              },
              {
                type: 'paragraph',
                text: 'Cards per Player: 5 tiles each\nDealing Pattern: Banker deals to each player\nDealer: Banker (chosen by dice for the hand)',
              },
            ],
          },
          {
            title: 'Variations',
            subtitle: 'Known ways this game changes',
            content: [
              {
                type: 'list',
                style: 'unordered',
                items: [
                  {
                    text: 'Domino version: Played with double-six dominoes; 3–6 players; five tiles each; discard three totalling multiple of 10; two remaining tiles score mod 10; beat the banker. Wilds 4-2 and 2-1.',
                  },
                  {
                    text: 'Card version (Ngau/Gnau): Played with 52-card deck; 2+ players; five cards each; choose three that sum to multiple of 10 or three-of-a-kind for scoring; two remaining cards give Ox power (face=10, 3s and 6s flexible). Hand ranks include Five Dukes, All-Small, Double-Ox.',
                  },
                ],
