          equipment: 'Double-six domino set\nTable space\nOptional: dice to choose banker',
          dealing: 'Cards per Player: 5 tiles each\nDealing Pattern: Banker deals to each player\nDealer: Banker (chosen by dice for the hand)',
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        rules: {
          objective: "Have a higher hand than the banker: after discarding three tiles that total a multiple of 10, the sum of the two remaining tiles (modulo 10) must beat the banker's total.",
          gameplay: '1. Banker: One player is chosen by dice as banker; sets betting limits and deals.\n2. Deal: Banker deals five tiles to each player; players place bets.\n3. Discard: Each player chooses three tiles that total a multiple of 10 and discards them; the 4-2 and 2-1 tiles are wild (count as 3 or 6). If a player cannot form a multiple-of-10 discard, they lose their bet; if the banker cannot, the banker pays all who did and others get bets back.\n4. Score: Sum the pips on the two remaining tiles and take the last digit (mod 10). Higher than banker wins; lower loses; tie pushes.\n5. Bank: If the banker made a discard, the bank passes right; otherwise the banker keeps the bank.',
          keyRules: [
            'Discard exactly three tiles whose pips sum to a multiple of 10; wilds 4-2 and 2-1 may stand for 3 or 6.',
            'Hand score is the sum of the two remaining tiles modulo 10.',
            "Beat the banker's score to win; tie is push.",
            'Banker who cannot discard pays all players who could; players who could not discard get their bets back.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
        strategy: {
          basic: 'Identify tiles that can form a multiple of 10; use wilds 4-2 and 2-1 as 3 or 6 when needed.',
          intermediate: 'Split the hand into odd- and even-pip tiles; (even+even+even), (odd+odd+even) can be multiples of 10; (odd+odd+odd) cannot.',
          advanced: 'With five odd tiles you cannot discard and lose; with four odds start from the one even tile; with three odds look for odd+odd+even; with two odds try two odds plus one even, or three evens; with one odd treat it as flexible; with no odds search among all five.',
          tips: [
            'Mental math: only even totals can be multiples of 10.',
            'If you cannot make a discard, you lose your bet; banker in that case pays all who could and returns stakes to those who could not.',
          ],
          hasPlaceholders: false,
        },
